articles.content_en:
Article 1: Where any person destroys electric power equipment under any of the following circumstances, it shall be deemed as "causing serious consequences" as stipulated in paragraph 1 of Article 119 of the Criminal Law, and the person shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than ten years, life imprisonment, or death penalty for the crime of destroying electric power equipment:
(1) causing the death of one or more persons, serious injury to three or more persons, or minor injury to ten or more persons;
(2) causing interruption of power supply to more than 10,000 users for more than six hours, thereby seriously affecting production and daily life;
(3) causing direct economic losses of more than one million yuan; or
(4) causing other serious consequences endangering public security.
